  "warnings": [
    "SAME 16 COLUMNS AS THE GROUND FLOOR, position for position - checked one by one against S-01 view2 and both footing plans. C2 at ง2/ง3/ค2/ค3, C1 everywhere else. The section sizes step down with height (S-03: C1 0.15x0.15 on both floors, C2 0.20x0.20 at ชั้นล่าง and 0.15x0.15 at ชั้นบน), but the positions do not move.",
    "B4 AND B4A APPEAR ONLY ON THIS FLOOR and only on the ง line. B4's grid1-to-grid2 run is 3.50 m, matching the 3.50 printed on S-04's B4 elevation exactly. B4A is recorded as TWO atomic segments (grid 2 to 3, then 3 to 4) per §4 because a C2 column stands at ง3 between them; note that S-04's B4A elevation dimensions the run 5.20 m overall, which is 2.20 + 3.00 - i.e. the mark is one continuous two-bay member and the split here is the extraction convention, not a physical joint. Anything summing B4A lengths should be aware of that.",
    "THE ง'' TO ง' STRIP IS THE POROUS PART OF THIS READING. On the ground floor that strip is a plain balcony; here it is the หลังคาไก่ +5.10 ม. porch roof, so hip lines, purlins and dashed framing are overlaid on the same area as the concrete beams. B2B and the two B2 stubs there are recorded with lower confidence, and the 1.80/1.60/1.80 sub-chain printed across the top dimensions the ROOF framing above, not concrete beams - it is deliberately not used to place any beam and no dummy grid was added for it.",
    "TWO DUMMY LINES IN THE GRID MASTER ARE USED ONLY BY THIS FLOOR: 1'' (1.70) carries the B2D/B2A line in the west bay and is confirmed by the printed 1.70 + 1.80 sub-chain closing on the 3.50 grid bay; 3' (6.00) carries the B3C beside the stair core and comes from the printed 0.30 right of grid 3. Neither splits anything on the ground floor, which is correct.",
    "B1ชานพัก KEEPS ITS THAI SUFFIX, per §0.3's rule that shortening must not create a collision. It is the stair-landing beam and is a genuinely different member from the plain B1 detailed on S-04; reducing it to B1 would cross-link it to B1's spec. Note S-04 details no B1ชานพัก, so this mark has no spec entry anywhere in the set - a real gap in the drawings, not a gap in this extraction.",
    "SLAB MARKS HERE ARE S1, S2 AND S3 - all three detailed on S-03. S1 and S2 do not appear on the ground floor at all and GS does not appear here, which is consistent: S1/S2 are the suspended precast-plank floors, GS is the slab on grade.",
    "SPEC JOIN: beam sections and reinforcement are on S-04, column/pedestal sections on S-03, slab sections on S-03. Not duplicated into this file, per §7's rule against repeating the spec on every occurrence.",
    "This file covers the LEFT view of หน้า21 only. The right view (แปลนคานรับหลังคา, โครงหลังคา) is a separate file per §3."
  ]
